/target
.env
# Build and packaging outputs. `dist/` holds the per-target binaries, and `npm/<platform>/bin/`
# holds the copy pack-npm.mjs places for `npm pack`. Neither is source: a binary committed here
# would be an artifact nobody can trace to a build. Patterns are file-level on purpose — `npm/*/bin/`
# would also have swallowed `npm/cli/bin/necropsy.js`, which *is* source, and CI would have run
# against a checkout with no launcher in it.
/dist
npm/*/bin/necropsy
npm/*/bin/necropsy.exe
npm/*/LICENSE
npm/*/README.md
node_modules/
*.tgz
# Cargo.lock is committed. This crate ships a binary, and `cargo build` without a lockfile
# resolves against whatever the registry index says today -- so "the same commit" is not the
# same program, and a CI green light can arrive from a dependency nobody reviewed. Library
# consumers ignore this file; only the binary's reproducibility depends on it.
# Project memory: this repo is public, and AGENTS.md records local environment
# facts and open threads. Loaded from disk by the agent either way.
AGENTS.md
